==Item Blacklists==
For your station map you should never map these items, outside of very special circumstances in which you should ask a maintainer.

    Nuclear Authentication Disk*
     >This is Spawned in the captain's locker, and that should be mapped instead
    Nuclear Authentication Codes
     >Required to detonate the nuclear bomb.
    Items with the [DEBUG] suffix
    Items with the [ADMIN] suffix 
    Supersynth
      >This is the DAW but better.
    Romerol
      >Do not add a major antag round start.
    Space-medipen
      >debug item, will remove itself immediately upon being initalized

=maintainer approval required items=

    Dual Port Vents (at your own risk, colouring is a pain and they might not work)
      >This note has been left standing for 2+ '''YEARS'''
    Digital Audio Workstation
      >Musician upgrade item
    Traitor uplink items
      >Clothing items are generally seen as fine, other items require maintainer approval
    Tier 2 and Tier 3 research unlocks
      >Ask for approval for each NON-STANDARD item, exceptions will be listed in departmental sections.

=Exceptions=
   Wt550 Should ALWAYS be mapped in somewhere in security, either armory or the HOS's office.
   the research director is allowed a drill
   ATMOS should have at least one spare Holofan projector for the senior engineer
   Engineering should NEVER get the protolathe.

==CD RULES==

   try to give every department their relevant records computer
   If your map is minimum 20 people turn it down to 15.
   Every department with a senior role should have a senior role office, this doesn't have to be a big space, it can just be a desk and a table. 
   A shooting range is preferred.
   Generally If you cannot make it in round (RCD use is allowed) do not map it in such a way